ed January 14, 2025. Weddle serves residential and commercial clients within the Portland Metropolitan region and surrounding areas of Northwest Oregon and Southwest Washington.","section":"Management Discussion and Analysis","block":51,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001376474-26-000616","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-24","reportDate":"2026-09-24","cik":"0001997403","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1997403/000137647426000616/zt_ex99z2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/e92ade0acdfa6a87fe0591a4051e90d438527aea903a05830fecedc4865eef81.bin","sha256":"e92ade0acdfa6a87fe0591a4051e90d438527aea903a05830fecedc4865eef81"}},{"id":"052f2a8a48180139b0e7c6a30e521e4cf650498ac215c817701f9d80b1a6ada4","quote":"·Landtec Construction Surveying, DBA Wallace Surveying Corporation, (“Wallace”) of West Palm Beach, Florida, acquired on April 2nd, 2025. Wallace is a well-established land survey company with thirty years of experience providing construction and land development surveys delivering accurate and reliable data that supports project planning and design for developers, contractors, engineers, and architect customers.","context":"·KJM Land Surveying, Inc. (“KJM”), a Pensacola, Florida land surveying firm acquired on January 22, 2025, provides a range of professional land surveying services, including boundary surveys, ALTA surveys, as-built surveys, topographic surveys, and elevation certificates to residential, commercial, and construction customers.","section":"Management Discussion and Analysis","block":52,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001376474-26-000616","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-24","reportDate":"2026-09-24","cik":"0001997403","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1997403/000137647426000616/zt_ex99z2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/e92ade0acdfa6a87fe0591a4051e90d43