mming and support fees increased by $5,096,209 to $5,785,640, reflecting direct costs of DaaS operations including subcontracted labor for survey projects, field equipment, and hosting costs; general and administrative costs increased by $7,720,177 to $9,322,830, reflecting consolidated overhead from the acquired subsidiaries; professional fees increased by $2,400,167 to $2,894,467 from legal, audit, and consulting costs associated with public-company reporting; amortization and depreciation increased by $2,223,116 to $2,594,305; stock-based","context":"Revenue increased by $7,090,624, or 316%, for the three months ended June 30, 2026 as compared to the same period of 2025, and increased by $14,357,289, or 425%, for the six months ended June 30, 2026 as compared to the same period of 2025. This increase was driven primarily by the Drone as a Service segment, which contributed $8,629,971 in Q2 2026 (Q2 2025: $1,580,582) and $16,442,433 for the six months ended June 30, 2026 (six months 2025: $1,983,348), reflecting the continued consolidation of the twenty-five land surveying and related field service operations acquired during 2025 and the first half of 2026. The Enterprise SaaS Software segment contributed $702,315 in Q2 2026 (Q2 2025: $661,080) and $1,292,172 for the six months ended June 30, 2026 (six months 2025: $1,393,968).","section":"Results of Operations — Summary Data (Six Months)","block":88,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001376474-26-000616","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-24","reportDate":"2026-09-24","cik":"0001997403","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1997403/000137647426000616/zt_ex99z2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/e92ade0acdfa6a87fe0591a4051e90d438527aea903a05830fecedc4865eef81.bin","sha256":"e92ade0acdfa6a87fe0591a4051e90d438527aea903a05830fecedc4865eef81"}},{"id":"f21d363c6a409e5e7a48ab7b4f40bfa76aea8acfc31f959a6132084b62491327","quote":"Ne